; DOMAIN: mathematics/algebra/commutative-algebra [CLOSED, derived 2026-08-02]; Claim: Commutative algebra studies commutative rings, modules, and ideals, providing the algebraic foundation for algebraic geometry and number theory. Key results: Hilbert basis theorem (Noetherian rings stable under polynomial extension); Noetherian rings with ACC on ideals and primary decomposition; localization of rings and modules at prime ideals; Nakayama's lemma (finitely generated module M with IM=M implies M=0 over local ring); Krull's principal ideal theorem (height of minimal prime over principal ideal ≤ 1); Krull dimension; flat modules and faithful flatness; tensor products and base change; integral extensions and going-up/going-down theorems; completions and the Artin-Rees lemma; the structure theorem for modules over PIDs. Bridges to algebraic_geometry (Spec R, affine schemes, structure sheaf), number_theory (Dedekind domains, rings of integers), and homological_algebra (flat/projective modules, Tor/Ext).;; Hilbert basis theorem: if R is Noetherian, then R[x] is Noetherian; every ideal in R[x] is finitely generated
(|- ((==> (&& (--> CommutativeRing $R) (--> Noetherian $R) (--> PolynomialRing $Rx (Polynomial $R)))) (--> Noetherian $Rx)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Noetherian ring: satisfies ascending chain condition on ideals; every ideal is finitely generated; primary decomposition exists for ideals
(|- ((==> (&& (--> CommutativeRing $R) (--> AscendingChainCondition $R) (--> FinitelyGenerated (IdealsOf $R)) (--> Exists (PrimaryDecomposition (IdealsOf $R))))) (--> NoetherianRing $R)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Localization: inverting elements at a multiplicative set S forms ring S^-1 R; modules localize to S^-1 M; local ring at prime ideal p
(|- ((==> (&& (--> CommutativeRing $R) (--> MultiplicativeSet $S $R) (--> RingOfFractions $SR (Invert $S $R)) (--> Module $M $R) (--> LocalizedModule $SM (Invert $S $M)))) (--> Localization $R $S $SR $SM)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Nakayama's lemma: if M is finitely generated over local ring (R,m) and mM=M, then M=0
(|- ((==> (&& (--> LocalRing $R $m) (--> FinitelyGeneratedModule $M $R) (--> Equals (Product $m $M) $M))) (--> ZeroModule $M)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Krull principal ideal theorem: height of a minimal prime ideal over a principal ideal is at most 1
(|- ((==> (&& (--> CommutativeRing $R) (--> PrincipalIdeal $I $R) (--> PrimeIdeal $P (MinimalPrimeOver $I $R)) (--> Height $P))) (--> KrullPrincipalIdealTheorem $R $P $I)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Krull dimension: supremum of lengths of chains of prime ideals in R
(|- ((==> (&& (--> CommutativeRing $R) (--> ChainOfPrimes $C $R) (--> Supremum (Length $C) (KrullDimension $R)))) (--> Defined (KrullDimension $R))) (stv 1.0 0.9))
;; Flat module: M is flat over R if tensoring with M preserves exact sequences; faithfully flat if additionally reflects exactness
(|- ((==> (&& (--> Module $M $R) (--> ExactSequence $E) (--> Preserves $M (Tensor $M) $E))) (--> FlatModule $M $R)) (stv 1.0 0.9))
